# Market brief parity, against the shared Vapor (MARKET_BRIEF_ENABLED unset):
# GET /v1/market/brief answers the disabled card; the push opt-in routes are
# not gated. Reset fixtures first, every run:
#   docker exec -i norviq-v2-schema-pg psql -U pg -d norviq < parity/market-brief-setup.sql
#   go run ./cmd/parity -a http://127.0.0.1:8081 -b http://127.0.0.1:18118 -jwt-secret parity-secret \
#     -cases parity/market-brief.jsonl -ignore requestId \
#     -headers Content-Type,Cache-Control,X-Frame-Options,X-Content-Type-Options,Referrer-Policy
# Run v2 with MARKET_BRIEF_ENABLED unset. The enabled card is in
# parity/market-brief-enabled.jsonl.
# Expected diffs (2026-10-30: 27 cases, 3 differ), all foundation-wide, not
# brief-specific:
# - "brief bad token": Vapor's reason is JWTKit's "Token parts count is not
#   3."; v2 says "Unauthorized" (same on every d.Auth.Scoped() route, e.g.
#   /v1/market/fx).
# - "prefs put malformed": the "Underlying error" tail of the DecodingError
#   reason is Foundation's NSError text in Vapor, Go's in v2.
# - "prefs put form": Vapor's URLEncodedFormDecoder reads "true" as a Bool;
#   swiftjson.decodeForm passes form values as JSON strings, so v2 answers
#   400. iOS and the web send JSON.
